id: pm-dpqa3h
title: "The agent token-surface harness from pm-a22j is wired into nothing, so output-size regressions like the 33k-token health check land undetected"
description: "scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs measures root help, per-command help, contracts payloads and MCP tools/list, and has a covering spec, but has no package.json script, no CI step and no committed baseline. Repo-wide search finds one reference outside the file itself, a historical CHANGELOG line."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli",ci-gate,observability,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-26T18:28:20.913Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T15:08:18.190Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T14:00:45.668Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "A package.json script runs the token-surface harness and a committed baseline artifact records the current surface; A static CI gate diffs measured against baseline and fails when growth exceeds the declared threshold, with a documented baseline-update path; The gate reproduces the currently measured values for health, validate, context, next, get and list-open so the baseline is verifiable"
goal: project management = context management
value: "Turns an already-built, already-tested measurement into a continuous ratchet, so token regressions are caught at authoring time instead of during a manual audit."
impact: Every agent-facing payload can grow without limit today; token cost is the scarcest resource in the agent loop.
outcome: "A committed token-surface baseline plus a static CI gate that fails on growth beyond a declared threshold, following the sdk-surface-snapshot precedent."
why_now: "pm health --check-only currently emits 132,585 B (~33k tokens) and is the diagnostic AGENTS.md routes agents to; the instrument that would have flagged it on the introducing commit exists and runs nowhere."
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Turned the dormant token-surface measurement into a versioned committed regression ratchet enforced by context quality CI and release gates.
expected_result: "Every measured agent-facing surface has a reproducible baseline, documented update path, and automated growth check."
actual_result: "Ninety-five surfaces and a seventeen-command representative corpus are checked; linked tests, context evaluation, and full coverage pass."
