close_reason: "Shipped a committed 95-surface token regression baseline, CI/release enforcement, documented update path, and expanded representative command corpus; linked tests, full 100% coverage, static quality, context evaluation, security scan, and dependency audit passed."
body: "## Problem\n\npm-a22j (closed) built scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs: it measures the\nfull agent-facing token surface — root help, every per-command help, the\ncontracts payload family, and the MCP tools/list payload — and emits JSON so a\nratchet can diff it. pm-ksca (closed) then added a covering spec for it.\n\nThe harness is wired into nothing. Repository-wide search for\n`measure-agent-token-surface` outside the script itself returns exactly one\nhit, a historical CHANGELOG line. It has no package.json script, no CI step,\nand no recorded baseline to diff against. Its own header comment tells the\nreader to \"re-run after each consolidation slice lands and diff against the\nrecorded baseline\" — a baseline that is not stored anywhere in the repo.\n\n## Consequence, measured 2026-07-26 on the live workspace\n\nNothing detects token-surface regressions, and they are present:\n\n| command | output | approx tokens |\n|---|---|---|\n| pm graph audit --summary | 1,534 B | ~383 |\n| pm list-open --limit 20 | 4,556 B | ~1,139 |\n| pm get pm-96h7 | 5,365 B | ~1,341 |\n| pm context --limit 10 | 6,195 B | ~1,548 |\n| pm next --limit 5 | 8,799 B | ~2,199 |\n| pm validate | 22,719 B | ~5,679 |\n| **pm health --check-only** | **132,585 B** | **~33,146** |\n\n`pm health --check-only` is the diagnostic AGENTS.md \"When Unsure\" routes\nagents to, and a single invocation costs roughly a sixth of a 200k context\nwindow. That specific regression is owned by pm-du93sr and `graph impact` by\npm-mfy1ux — this item owns the reason such regressions land and persist\nundetected: the instrument that would have caught them on the commit that\nintroduced them runs nowhere.\n\n## Why this is a child of pm-5t33or, not a duplicate\n\npm-5t33or owns the forward design: every command declares a default output\nceiling in its contract and degrades deterministically when it would exceed it.\nThat is the destination. This item is the enabling tranche that can ship\nindependently and immediately: take the harness that already exists and already\nhas a spec, record a committed baseline, and fail CI when the surface grows\nbeyond it. It requires no contract changes and no command behaviour changes,\nand it makes pm-5t33or's rollout measurable slice by slice instead of\nretrospective.\n\n## Direction (not a mandate for the fix)\n\nAdd a package.json script, commit a baseline JSON artifact next to the\nsdk-surface-snapshot baseline that already follows this pattern, and add a\nstatic CI gate that diffs current against baseline with an allowed-growth\nthreshold and a documented update path. The sdk-surface-snapshot gate is the\nworking precedent for exactly this shape."
